; st.lab.test: the subdomain_takeover targets (test_corpus/README.md). Each target is a name in
; this zone (served by dns-res, the scanner's resolver). Its subdomains point into stand-in
; provider zones (provider-live.db / provider-gone.db) whose web answers come from the
; `providers` container (nginx/providers.conf). Nothing here is reachable from the internet.
$ORIGIN st.lab.test.
$TTL 300
@        IN SOA ns.dns.lab.test. hostmaster.st.lab.test. 1 7200 3600 1209600 300
@        IN NS  ns.dns.lab.test.
; every target itself: an ordinary A record (no CNAME)
s3pos      IN A 192.0.2.80
azpos      IN A 192.0.2.80
bbpos      IN A 192.0.2.80
surgepos   IN A 192.0.2.80
dangpos    IN A 192.0.2.80
chainpos   IN A 192.0.2.80
claimed    IN A 192.0.2.80
edgecase   IN A 192.0.2.80
plain      IN A 192.0.2.80
scope      IN A 192.0.2.80
; --- s3pos: CT-listed name -> S3 bucket that no longer exists (NoSuchBucket) -> HIGH
assets.s3pos     IN CNAME assets.s3pos.st.lab.test.s3.amazonaws.com.
; --- azpos: CT-listed name -> Azure App Service name that was deleted (NXDOMAIN) -> HIGH
app.azpos        IN CNAME azpos-app.azurewebsites.net.
; --- bbpos: NOT in CT; "docs" is one of the ten common names -> Bitbucket "Repository not found" -> HIGH
docs.bbpos       IN CNAME bbpos.bitbucket.io.
; --- surgepos: CT-listed www -> Surge.sh "project not found" -> HIGH
www.surgepos     IN CNAME surgepos.surge.sh.
; --- dangpos: CT-listed name -> a name that does not exist at an UNLISTED provider -> LOW (dangling_cname)
old.dangpos      IN CNAME site.gone-cdn.test.
; --- chainpos: two hops: cdn -> edge (own zone) -> S3 website endpoint, bucket gone -> HIGH
cdn.chainpos     IN CNAME edge.chainpos.st.lab.test.
edge.chainpos    IN CNAME chainpos-media.s3-website-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com.
; --- claimed: CNAMEs into listed providers whose resources EXIST -> NOTHING
docs.claimed     IN CNAME claimed.bitbucket.io.
files.claimed    IN CNAME files.claimed.st.lab.test.s3.amazonaws.com.
env.claimed      IN CNAME claimed.eu-west-1.elasticbeanstalk.com.
; --- edgecase: GitHub Pages fingerprint ("Edge case" provider, not listed) and a listed
;     fingerprint served by an UNLISTED provider -> NOTHING
blog.edgecase    IN CNAME edgecase.github.io.
help.edgecase    IN CNAME edgecase.pages-host.test.
; --- plain: A records, a CT name deleted from DNS (NXDOMAIN, no CNAME), and a CNAME to a
;     missing name inside the owner's own domain (nobody else can create it) -> NOTHING
www.plain        IN A 192.0.2.81
api.plain        IN A 192.0.2.81
legacy.plain     IN CNAME gone.plain.st.lab.test.
; --- scope: its CT answer also lists names OUTSIDE scope.st.lab.test, two of them dangling
;     (a sibling target's app.azpos, and the look-alike evilscope). Never asked -> NOTHING
evilscope        IN CNAME evil-app.azurewebsites.net.
